.TH OROC-TOOLING-KOTLIN 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.2.0" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-tooling\-kotlin \- Export and prepare Oro editor compilation models.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc tooling kotlin [options] [<project\-dir>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Export and prepare Oro editor compilation models.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-prepare\fR
compile resources and JVM classes for analysis
.TP
\fB\-\-variant=<name>\fR
Android variant (default devDebug)
.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\fR
regenerate the Android editor project
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
resolve dependencies without network access
.TP
\fB\-\-config=<path>\fR
explicit oro.toml or oro.ini
.TP
\fB\-\-classpath\fR
print only the resolved editor classpath
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
show help
.SH NOTES
.PP
Prints the versioned JSON model by default. Uses Oro configuration and Gradle task providers.
.PP
Preparation does not assemble, sign, install, or compile native libraries.
.PP
Gradle, a compatible JDK, Android SDK packages and dependency artifacts must be installed.
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1), oroc\-tooling(1)
